  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. A long session (WBS 8.5) of 52 inputs whose only fight, against two harpies, comes late, from input 38, after 37 inputs of social and quest play. The pilgrimage quest is already active at stage 1 in the starting state, so the first input that touches it is an advance (input 4), not a start; it reaches stage 4 at input 33 and completes at input 47. Four quests in all: the fevered monk completes, the storeroom thief fails at input 27 because Ansa keeps Tam's secret, and the high bell (max_stage 1) completes. Three NPCs: the abbot climbs three steps from unfriendly to allied (inputs 14, 48 and 50), and Brother Tam and Sorin each go down one step and later back up one, so both end where they began. Frost-lilies go 2, 3, 0 at inputs 2, 9 and 16; rope goes 1, 2, 1 at inputs 32 and 35, so the climb down at input 49 uses the rope left behind, not one in the pack. Ansa is a caster with 3 spell slots and spends one, on herself, at input 45, so input 51 should find 2 left. The ice bridge at input 6 is rolled with scenario disadvantage. Inputs 38 to 44 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
}
